### Strategic Horizons & Post-Silicon Paradigm Transitions
Analyzes future technological implications as silicon CMOS scaling approaches physical limits:
- **Post-Silicon Computing Substrates**: Transitioning toward optical computing, 3D GAAFET/CFET architectures, and room-temperature superconductors.
- **Artificial General Intelligence Scaling**: Extrapolating compute trajectories toward human-level and superhuman AI capabilities.
- **Socio-Economic Abundance Paradigms**: Exploring economic models adapted to near-zero marginal cost information and automated physical production.

## Macroeconomic, Geopolitical, and Planetary Phase Transitions

The sustained acceleration of computation, biotechnology, and robotics projected by the Law of Accelerating Returns leads inexorably to qualitative phase transitions across human civilization. When cognitive automation decouples economic production from biological human labor, the classical production function undergoes a radical structural singularity:

$$Y(t) = A(t) K(t)^\alpha L(t)^{1-\alpha} \xrightarrow{L(t) \to \infty \text{ (cognitive compute)}} Y(t) \approx A(t) K(t)$$

In this AK-type hyper-growth regime, the constraint on economic expansion shifts entirely from labor availability and human education cycles to energy production, raw material extraction, and thermal heat dissipation.

